---
// Research section. Accessible to a smart non-scientist, respectable to a
// specialist. No proprietary platform names, acronyms, or invented metrics.
const areas = [
  {
    no: '01',
    title: 'Injury to the newborn brain',
    meta: 'Prematurity · hypoxia · cerebral palsy',
    body: 'When a baby is born early or deprived of oxygen, the brain can be injured in ways that lead to lifelong conditions such as cerebral palsy. She models these insults in human tissue to understand the damage and search for ways to protect and repair it.',
  },
  {
    no: '02',
    title: '22q11.2 deletion syndrome',
    meta: 'Interneuron balance · mechanism',
    body: 'A small missing piece of one chromosome carries an outsized risk for the developing brain. She studies how it disrupts the cells that keep brain circuits in balance, and what might be done to restore them.',
  },
  {
    no: '03',
    title: 'Epilepsy and circuit balance',
    meta: 'Excitation · inhibition · circuits',
    body: 'Healthy brains hold a careful balance between signals that excite and signals that calm. When that balance breaks, seizures can follow. Her models reveal how the balance is set during development, and how it fails.',
  },
  {
    no: '04',
    title: 'From model to medicine',
    meta: 'Screening · therapeutic testing',
    body: 'Human models are only worthwhile if they point to treatments. She builds the screening and testing steps a candidate must pass on its way from the dish toward patients.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="research">
  <div class="wrap wrap-wide reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
    <h2>Growing the human brain in a dish, to understand it and to heal it.</h2>

    <p class="lead measure">
      Brain organoids are small, self-organizing, three-dimensional models of human brain tissue,
      grown from stem cells. Assembloids join organoids together so different brain regions can
      meet and connect, letting her study the developing brain directly.
    </p>

    <div class="index-list">
      {areas.map((a) => (
        <article class="row reveal">
          <span class="mono no">{a.no}</span>
          <div class="row-main">
            <h3>{a.title}</h3>
            <p>{a.body}</p>
          </div>
          <span class="mono row-meta">{a.meta}</span>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="research-note measure">
      Why it matters: the disorders she works on touch some of the most vulnerable patients there
      are, often with few options today. Better human models are a faster, more honest path to the
      treatments those patients need.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .index-list {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    border-top: 1.5px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.4rem;
    padding: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.9rem) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    position: relative;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 780px) {
    .row { grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr 15rem; align-items: baseline; }
  }

  .row .no { color: var(--accent); padding-top: 0.35rem; }

  .row-main h3 { font-size: var(--step-2); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .row-main p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 52ch; }

  .row-meta {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    padding-top: 0.35rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 780px) {
    .row-meta { text-align: right; }
  }

  /* subtle technical hover: cobalt tick on the left */
  .row::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -1rem;
    top: 0;
    width: 3px;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--accent);
    transform: scaleY(0);
    transform-origin: top;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }
  .row:hover::before { transform: scaleY(1); }

  .research-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    padding-left: var(--space-m);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
